From: Flow contributors <flow@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: litex: read response CSRs with explicit 32-bit accesses

On Breeze RV64, memcpy_fromio uses ld for the 128-bit response window.
The 32-bit CSR bridge drops the upper word, so a valid CMD55 response
(0x120) becomes zero and mmc_app_cmd rejects it with -EOPNOTSUPP.
Use four litex_read32 accesses, preserving the existing response order.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/litex_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/litex_mmc.c
@@ -173,11 +173,13 @@
 
 	if (response_len != SD_CTL_RESP_NONE) {
 		/*
-		 * NOTE: this matches the semantics of litex_read32()
-		 * regardless of underlying arch endianness!
+		 * LiteX CSRs require 32-bit transactions. memcpy_fromio() can
+		 * issue 64-bit loads on RV64, losing the upper response word
+		 * on a 32-bit CSR bridge. Keep the hardware word order.
 		 */
-		memcpy_fromio(host->resp,
-			      host->sdcore + LITEX_CORE_CMDRSP, 0x10);
+		for (unsigned int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(host->resp); i++)
+			host->resp[i] = litex_read32(host->sdcore +
+						   LITEX_CORE_CMDRSP + 4 * i);
 	}
 
 	if (!host->app_cmd && cmd == SD_SEND_RELATIVE_ADDR)
